// ---- epoll over WSAPoll ----
// epoll_create1 makes a descriptor of kind 4 whose page (word 2 of its table entry) holds the registered sockets, 16 bytes each (the
// descriptor, the events, the caller's data word); word 3 counts them, word 4 is a spin lock. epoll_ctl edits the registry, epoll_wait
// polls the registered sockets (level triggered, as the standard library asks for) and fills 12-byte packed epoll_event records. A
// registered socket that was closed without being removed is dropped by the next wait. Linux events: IN 1, PRI 2, OUT 4, ERR 8,
// HUP 16, RDHUP 8192; WSAPoll reports an abortive close as HUP, a graceful one as readable (the read returns 0).

