// The Windows-only system call 4006, `systemRoots`: the DER of every certificate in the user's ROOT store (the system's trusted roots),
// each as a 32-bit length and the bytes, in the buffer of `size` bytes. Returns the bytes the records take (more than `size` when
// the buffer was too small: none was stored past it, and the caller asks again with that much) or -errno. The standard library's
// trust store (abla/tls/pure) reads them where Linux reads a bundle file.
// The calls through an address GetProcAddress gave (the two shapes crypt32's functions take): declared here, not imported from abla/unsafe/native,
// which this module does not link against.
